    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I've always been more comfortable with physics and history, not maths. I remember being good at basic arithmetic but struggled with algebra. I enjoy the patterns in maths but often feel overwhelmed. I see it as a series of rules that need to be followed, and if I mess up, things get messy. I've always preferred learning through doing rather than memorizing formulas.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Yes, definitely. I get anxious when faced with a new equation or problem. It feels like I'm trying to piece together something I don’t fully understand. I often freeze up, especially if there’s a lot of variables or steps. It’s not fear of failure, but more a feeling of being lost in the logic. I think the anxiety comes from not having a strong foundation early on.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I used a chatbot to help me understand a quadratic equation. It explained the steps clearly, and I found it helpful. It didn’t solve the problems for me, which I appreciated. It helped me visualize the process. I still made mistakes, but it gave me more confidence. I’ve used it a few times now and it’s become a useful tool.",
