    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can offer personalized explanations and step-by-step guidance. They can adapt to different learning paces and styles. They can help students explore problems in a conversational way. They can also offer instant feedback. This makes math less intimidating and more interactive. It's a tool to support, not replace, teachers."
